<title>USA: Option Care acquires Oklahoma facility.</title>
<headline>Option Care acquires Oklahoma facility.</headline>
<dateline>BANNOCKBURN, Ill. 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Option Care Inc said Tuesday it acquired Addison Home Care Inc, its franchised operation in Oklahoma City.</p>
<p>The transaction was structured as a stock acquisition and accounted for as a pooling of interests, the company said.</p>
<p>Addison had revenues of $3.3 million in 1995 and has a staff of 30 people. Its business is focused on therapy niche markets, mainly in pediactrics and maternal child care, the company said.</p>
<p>Option Care said it expects to expand its presence in Oklahoma City.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
